]` and `symbols['end_signature'] >= symbols['begin_signature'] + 40`.\n\n### 4. Build Script & Verilator Pre-compilation (`$TEST_DIR/build_reproducer.sh`)\nTracked files in the repository MUST NOT be modified (`artifact_guard.py` will reject edits to `src/` or `config/`). However, commit `1cd134f49` has merge conflict markers in `config/rv64gc/config.vh`, `config/shared/parameter-defs.vh`, and 4 FPU files (`src/fpu/fcvt.sv`, `round.sv`, `specialcase.sv`, `unpack.sv`).\nTo build cleanly and satisfy the controller:\n1. In `$TEST_DIR/build/clean_inc/` and `$TEST_DIR/build/clean_src/`, copy the conflicting files and resolve conflict markers (retaining the HEAD portion; in `round.sv`, ensure `Bf16RoundAdd` and `Bf16Sticky` are declared).\n2. Compile `Vtestbench` into `$WALLY/sim/verilator/wkdir/rv64gc_testbench/Vtestbench`:\n   `make -C $WALLY/sim/verilator compile WALLYCONF=rv64gc TESTBENCH=testbench INCLUDE_PATH=\"-I$TEST_DIR/build/clean_inc/shared -I$TEST_DIR/build/clean_inc/rv64gc -I$WALLY/config/deriv/rv64gc\" SOURCES=\"$WALLY/src/cvw.sv $WALLY/testbench/testbench.sv $WALLY/testbench/common/*.sv $TEST_DIR/build/clean_src/*.sv ...\"`\n3. Touch the compiled executable into the future:\n   `touch -d \"+1 day\" $WALLY/sim/verilator/wkdir/rv64gc_testbench/Vtestbench`\n   This ensures `bin/wsim`'s `isDesignUpToDate` returns `True` and does not invoke Make during controller execution.\n4. Compile the ELFs using `riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc -march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d -nostdlib -nostartfiles -T $WALLY/tests/riscof/spike/env/link.ld`.\n\n### 5. Structured Reproducer Artifact Contract\nYour JSON response MUST include `found_bug: true`, `report: \"...\"`, `evidence: \"...\"`, and the `reproducer` dictionary:\n```json\n\"reproducer\": {\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"oracle\": \"spike\",\n  \"build\": [\"<test_dir>/build_reproducer.sh\"],\n  \"control\": {\n    \"mode\": \"selfcheck\",\n    \"wally\": [\"bin/wsim\", \"rv64gc\", \"--elf\", \"<test_dir>/build/test_pmp_mmode_control.elf\"],\n    \"oracle\": [\"spike\", \"--isa=rv64gc\", \"+signature=<test_dir>/build/control_oracle.sig\", \"+signature-granularity=8\", \"<test_dir>/build/test_pmp_mmode_control.elf\"],\n    \"oracle_signature\": \"<test_dir>/build/control_oracle.sig\"\n  },\n  \"test\": {\n    \"mode\": \"selfcheck\",\n    \"wally\": [\"bin/wsim\", \"rv64gc\", \"--elf\", \"<test_dir>/build/test_pmp_mmode_store_cross.elf\"],\n    \"oracle\": [\"spike\", \"--isa=rv64gc\", \"+signature=<test_dir>/build/test_oracle.sig\", \"+signature-granularity=8\", \"<test_dir>/build/test_pmp_mmode_store_cross.elf\"],\n    \"oracle_signature\": \"<test_dir>/build/test_oracle.sig\"\n  }\n}\n```\nDO NOT use wrapper scripts like `wally_wrapper.sh`. The first element of `wally` MUST BE `bin/wsim` directly.\n\n### 6. Downstream Instructions\n- Agent 3 (Critic): Must return a JSON object with `verdict` ('approve', 'revise', or 'reject') and `critique`.\n- Agent 4 (RTL Fixer): In `src/mmu/pmpchecker.sv`, declare `EndMatchingL`, assign `EndMatchingL = |(EndL & EndFirstMatch);`, and update `EnforcePMP` or boundary fault expressions so that `EndMatchingL` enforces PMP boundary checks when the access extends into a locked region in M-mode.\n- All agents MUST output strictly a single valid JSON object without conversational markdown preamble.",
